365
00:12:46,300 --> 00:12:46,600
Yep,

366
00:12:46,880 --> 00:12:48,520
immunoglobulin heavy chain.

367
00:12:49,040 --> 00:12:49,260
Okay,

368
00:12:49,660 --> 00:12:50,660
and guess what sits

369
00:12:50,660 --> 00:12:51,860
on chromosome 18?

370
00:12:52,980 --> 00:12:53,620
BCL2.

371
00:12:54,100 --> 00:12:54,740
You have to know

372
00:12:54,740 --> 00:12:55,520
that BCL2

373
00:12:55,520 --> 00:12:56,760
sits on chromosome 18.

374
00:12:57,280 --> 00:12:57,480
Well,

375
00:12:57,520 --> 00:12:58,140
you would know that

376
00:12:58,140 --> 00:12:59,940
because of the 14-18 translocation

377
00:12:59,940 --> 00:13:01,220
you know that BCL2

378
00:13:01,220 --> 00:13:02,820
is involved in follicular lymphoma.

379
00:13:02,980 --> 00:13:03,740
So these are some things

380
00:13:03,740 --> 00:13:04,440
to be aware of.

381
00:13:05,040 --> 00:13:05,240
Now,

382
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:06,420
this translocation,

383
00:13:06,780 --> 00:13:07,680
when BCL2

384
00:13:07,680 --> 00:13:09,000
goes to the immunoglobulin

385
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,080
heavy chain region

386
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:11,180
because we're dealing

387
00:13:11,180 --> 00:13:11,960
with B cells,

388
00:13:12,800 --> 00:13:13,560
this is occurring

389
00:13:13,560 --> 00:13:14,240
in B cells,

390
00:13:14,640 --> 00:13:15,760
then what's going to happen

391
00:13:15,760 --> 00:13:16,660
